        meaning02: '<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr><th scope="col">a</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>x</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table> C2-B-171: a tab after `=` keeps the header cell mark, as a space does; 0.1 read `|=` and a tab as a data cell whose text starts with `=` and the tab.',
