        kind: "escape",
        group: "rulings of 17 November",
        from: "|{>}{^} a |\n",
        to: "|\\{>}{^} a |\n",
        meaning02: '<table>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td style="text-align: right;">{^} a</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table> C2-B-171, C2-B-182: a cell prefix takes a run of glued brace blocks, with the marks only at the start of the first; 0.1 read every glued run in a cell prefix, such as `{>}{^}` or `{.a}{.b}`, as cell text.',
        toolEntry: "U-305",
        silent: true
